   "source": [
    "### 1. Answer\n",
    "Even for a random player with an average of 10 games played of Breakout, it is uncommon for him to have an average score of 2.0 or greater. With a normal distribution model (mean = 1.330, sd = 0.417), the probability that the average score for 10 games of Breakout is 2.0 or greater is around 6.9% (and the simulated result was 8.0%). The 90th percentile is around 1.87, so just the top 10% of random players will average above that score."
   ]
